  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "We have a graph with NNN nodes (numbered 111 through NNN). For each valid uuu and vvv, there is an undirected edge between nodes uuu and vvv if vvv is a prime divisor of uuu or uuu is a prime divisor of vvv.\n\nYou should answer QQQ queries. In each query, you should find the length of the shortest path between two given nodes aaa and bbb or determine that there is no path between them.\n\n**Note**: Because of large I/O, please use fast I/O methods.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains a single integer QQQ.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers aaa and bbb describing a query.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, print a single line containing one integer - the distance between the nodes or −1-1−1 if the nodes are not connected.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,Q≤1061 \\le N, Q \\le 10^61≤N,Q≤106",
      "2≤a,b≤N2 \\le a, b \\le N2≤a,b≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "20\n3\n2 3\n2 6\n2 9",
        "output": "2\n1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nFor a=2a = 2a=2 and b=9b = 9b=9, one possible shortest path is 2→6→3→92 \\rightarrow 6 \\rightarrow 3 \\rightarrow 92→6→3→9."
      }
    ]
  },
